#!/bin/bash
# yt: the pipeline from the terminal (no AI).
#   yt status | yt watch [SECONDS] | yt run NAME cut|storyboard|render [--here|--fast] | yt log NAME | yt open NAME | yt host
#   --fast: ignore PRIORITY=background for this run (all cores, louder); a stage already running can't be moved off it
#   hand-off (work Mac): yt bundle NAME [DIR] | yt import NAME VIDEO [CHAPTERS]     home Mac: yt clean-renders
#   YouTube: yt run NAME youtube (draft, beside the render) | yt youtube NAME (rebuild) | yt thumb NAME [N|frames] | yt music NAME [samples|N|none] | yt shorten NAME (Bitly) | yt published NAME URL
s="$0"   # follow the ~/.local/bin/yt link (install.sh) back to this folder, where lib.sh is
while [ -L "$s" ]; do t="$(readlink "$s")"; case "$t" in /*) s="$t" ;; *) s="$(dirname "$s")/$t" ;; esac; done
. "$(cd "$(dirname "$s")" && pwd)/lib.sh"
case "${1:-status}" in
  status)   # every video, its stage and progress (render: from the log; cut and storyboard: ~ estimated from earlier runs)
    python3 "$PIPE/progress.py" "$ROOT" ;;
  watch)    # yt status every N seconds (default 10) until Ctrl-C
    while :; do clear; date '+%H:%M:%S'; python3 "$PIPE/progress.py" "$ROOT"; sleep "${2:-10}"; done ;;
  run)
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] && [ -n "${3:-}" ] || { echo "yt run NAME cut|storyboard|render [--here|--fast]"; exit 2; }
    mkdir -p "$ROOT/videos/$2/pipeline"
    nohup bash "$PIPE/stage.sh" "$2" "$3" "${4:-}" >> "$ROOT/videos/$2/pipeline/stage.log" 2>&1 &
    echo "started $3 for $2${4:+ ($4)} (log: videos/$2/pipeline/stage.log)" ;;
  host)   # can the home Mac take a render right now?
    if [ -z "$RENDER_HOST_DIR" ]; then echo "no render host set: renders run on this Mac (install.sh --render-host DIR sets one)"; exit 0; fi
    python3 "$PIPE/remote-render.py" --check --host "$RENDER_HOST_DIR" ;;
  bundle)   # the render bundle as one zip (default ~/Desktop) to carry to the home Mac by hand
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] || { echo "yt bundle NAME [DIR]"; exit 2; }
    python3 "$PIPE/remote-render.py" --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" --zip "${3:-$HOME/Desktop}" ;;
  import)   # the finished video back from the home Mac: check, deliver, mark done
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] && [ -n "${3:-}" ] || { echo "yt import NAME VIDEO.mp4 [chapters.txt]"; exit 2; }
    out="$(python3 "$PIPE/import-render.py" "$ROOT/videos/$2" "$3" ${4:+"$4"})" || { echo "$out"; exit 1; }
    echo "$out"
    D="$(echo "$out" | awk -F'\t' '$1=="DELIVERED"{print $2}')"
    state_set "$2" done "rendered on the home Mac (hand-off)"
    if [ -f "$ROOT/videos/$2/youtube/metadata.json" ]; then   # the metadata's times against the real video
      F="$D/$(basename "$3")"; python3 "$SK/scripts/youtube-meta.py" check --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" --video "$F" \
        || echo "the video's length differs from what youtube/ was timed for: rerun yt youtube $2 and check the chapters"
    fi
    notify "YouTube edit: $2" "Imported and delivered to $D." "$D"
    echo "done. On the home Mac, yt clean-renders removes the bundle there." ;;
  clean-renders)   # the home Mac: remove finished hand-off and remote jobs from videos/_render-inbox
    for d in "$ROOT"/videos/_render-inbox/*/; do
      [ -f "$d/status.json" ] || continue
      st="$(python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(open(sys.argv[1])).get("stage",""))' "$d/status.json")"
      case "$st" in done|failed) rm -rf "$d" && echo "removed $(basename "$d") ($st)" ;; *) echo "kept $(basename "$d") ($st)" ;; esac
    done ;;
  youtube)   # rebuild youtube/YOUTUBE.md from metadata.json + the Bitly links in links.tsv (no AI)
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] || { echo "yt youtube NAME"; exit 2; }
    python3 "$SK/scripts/youtube-meta.py" build --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" ;;
  music)   # the music pass: "yt music NAME" (where it stands, opens MUSIC-REVIEW.html), "yt music NAME samples" (rebuild
           # the samples from music/cand-N.wav), "yt music NAME N" / "yt music NAME none" (the pick; resumes a render
           # that is waiting for it). NAME is a video here or a job in videos/_render-inbox/.
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] || { echo "yt music NAME [samples|N|none]"; exit 2; }
    if [ -f "$ROOT/videos/_render-inbox/$2/job.json" ]; then D="$ROOT/videos/_render-inbox/$2"; else D="$ROOT/videos/$2"; fi
    [ -d "$D" ] || { echo "no video or render job named $2"; exit 2; }
    case "${3:-}" in
      "") python3 "$SK/scripts/music.py" status --project "$D"
          [ -f "$D/MUSIC-REVIEW.html" ] && command -v open >/dev/null && open "$D/MUSIC-REVIEW.html"; exit 0 ;;
      samples) python3 "$SK/scripts/music.py" samples --project "$D"; exit $? ;;
      none) python3 "$SK/scripts/music.py" none --project "$D" || exit 1 ;;
      *[!0-9]*) echo "yt music NAME [samples|N|none]"; exit 2 ;;
      *) python3 "$SK/scripts/music.py" choose --project "$D" --pick "$3" || exit 1 ;;
    esac
    if [ "$D" = "$ROOT/videos/_render-inbox/$2" ]; then
      if grep -q '"awaiting-music"' "$D/status.json" 2>/dev/null; then
        nohup bash "$PIPE/render-host-job.sh" "$2" --from music >> "$D/render-host.log" 2>&1 &
        echo "mixing and delivering $2 (a notification comes when it's in out/)"
      else
        echo "recorded; the render mixes it in at its music step"
      fi
    elif grep -q '"awaiting-music"' "$D/state.json" 2>/dev/null; then
      MUSIC_FROM=1 nohup bash "$PIPE/stage.sh" "$2" render >> "$D/pipeline/stage.log" 2>&1 &
      echo "mixing and delivering $2 (a notification comes when it's done)"
    else
      echo "recorded; the render mixes it in at its music step"
    fi ;;
  thumb)   # (re)render the thumbnail options in metadata.json in the profile's brand, then rebuild YOUTUBE.md;
           # "yt thumb NAME 2" only option 2, "yt thumb NAME frames" a fresh candidate sheet (youtube/frames.jpg)
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] || { echo "yt thumb NAME [N|frames]"; exit 2; }
    case "${3:-}" in
      frames) python3 "$SK/scripts/thumbnail.py" frames --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" ;;
      "") python3 "$SK/scripts/thumbnail.py" render --project "$ROOT/videos/$2"; python3 "$SK/scripts/youtube-meta.py" build --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" | head -1 ;;
      *[!0-9]*) echo "yt thumb NAME [N|frames]"; exit 2 ;;
      *) python3 "$SK/scripts/thumbnail.py" render --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" --option "$3"; python3 "$SK/scripts/youtube-meta.py" build --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" | head -1 ;;
    esac
    [ -f "$ROOT/videos/$2/youtube/thumbnails.jpg" ] && command -v open >/dev/null && open "$ROOT/videos/$2/youtube/thumbnails.jpg" || true ;;
  shorten)   # Bitly links through the video's profile account (HubSpot only), then rebuild. --hubspot confirms an inbox
             # video whose profile was only assumed is HubSpot content.
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] || { echo "yt shorten NAME [--hubspot]"; exit 2; }
    case "${3:-}" in ""|--hubspot) ;; *) echo "yt shorten NAME [--hubspot]"; exit 2 ;; esac
    python3 "$SK/scripts/youtube-meta.py" shorten --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" ${3:+--confirm-profile} ;;
  published)   # record the YouTube link and date in catalog/VIDEOS.md
    [ -n "${2:-}" ] && [ -n "${3:-}" ] || { echo "yt published NAME https://youtu.be/..."; exit 2; }
    python3 "$SK/scripts/youtube-meta.py" published --project "$ROOT/videos/$2" --url "$3" ;;
  log) tail -n "${3:-40}" "$ROOT/videos/$2/pipeline/stage.log" ;;
  open) for f in REVIEW-B.html REVIEW-A.html; do [ -f "$ROOT/videos/$2/$f" ] && { open "$ROOT/videos/$2/$f"; exit 0; }; done; echo "no review page yet" ;;
  *) echo "yt status | yt watch [S] | yt run NAME STAGE [--here|--fast] | yt log NAME [LINES] | yt open NAME | yt host | yt bundle NAME | yt import NAME VIDEO | yt clean-renders | yt youtube NAME | yt thumb NAME [N|frames] | yt music NAME [samples|N|none] | yt shorten NAME | yt published NAME URL"; exit 2 ;;
esac
